{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310779,"nonce":"tu7y0i8ZvoN1GX8+Pg3zvlvPJq8=","title":"MEASURED: LLVM is ~172MB of the 223MB rayzor binary; the existing compiler/llvm-dynamic feature drops it to 51MB (41MB stripped). Both ...","message":"**MEASURED 2026-08-17 at `64993625`, macOS arm64, LLVM 21.1.2 (homebrew).**\n\n| build | size |\n|---|---|\n| static LLVM (current default) | **223.3 MB** |\n| static + `strip -x` | 199.6 MB |\n| **dynamic LLVM** (`--features compiler/llvm-dynamic`) | **51.2 MB** |\n| dynamic + `strip -x` | **40.9 MB** |\n\nSo **LLVM is ~172MB of the 223MB.** The switch ALREADY EXISTS —\n`llvm-dynamic = [\"llvm-sys/force-dynamic\"]` in compiler/Cargo.toml — but is\ndocumented only as a Debian/Ubuntu workaround (their `llvm-\u003cv\u003e-dev` lists Polly\nas a static component but ships no `libPolly.a`), not as the dominant size\nlever. Verified on the dynamic build: default JIT path runs, `--llvm --release`\nruns, `otool -L` binds `/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/libLLVM.dylib`.\n\n**THE DECISION IS DISTRIBUTION, NOT BUILD CONFIG.** LLVM's C++ ABI is not\nstable across majors, so a binary built against 21 will not load 20 or 22.\nDynamic suits anything with a package manager (homebrew/apt/dev checkout —\ndeclare `llvm@21`) and also cuts link time; static suits a standalone download.\nBoth shapes are supported by the existing flag, so carry both rather than pick.\n\n**COMPOSITION of the static binary** (`size -m`): `__TEXT` 195MB (`__text`\n136MB code, `__const` 52MB), `__LINKEDIT` 36MB (symbol table, 266,721 symbols).\nSymbol attribution is dominated by `ZN4llvm*`, libc++ `ZNSt3*`, and `aws-lc-rs`\n(via `rustls` \u003c- `rayzor-runtime`, for sys.ssl).\n\n**OTHER PROFILE LEVERS:**\n- `strip = \"debuginfo\"` buys **NOTHING** — release carries no debug info\n  (`strip -S` changed the size by 0). The 24MB is the LOCAL SYMBOL TABLE, which\n  `strip = true` removes at the cost of function names in panic backtraces.\n- `panic = \"abort\"` is **RULED OUT**: 13 `catch_unwind` sites, including the\n  runtime's FFI panic guard (panics -\u003e Haxe exceptions) and Cranelift's define\n  guard.\n- `codegen-units` is unset (release default 16). Untried. Note it interacts\n  with the existing `[profile.release.package.compiler] opt-level = 2` pin,\n  which works around an LLVM optimiser bug causing infinite loops in TAST\n  lowering — confirm that does not resurface.\n\n**NOT VERIFIED:** only `hello.hx` on both backends. The `llvm-dynamic` path is\nexercised far less than the static one; run the full suite before making it a\ndefault anywhere.\n\n- Index summary moved from MEMORY.md (2026-10-18): LLVM is ~172MB of 223MB. `--features compiler/llvm-dynamic` → 51MB. Trade-off is DISTRIBUTION. `panic=abort` RULED OUT (13 catch_unwind).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `perf_binary_size_llvm_is_172_of_223mb` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}